{
	"_source": "S4 (VR24-209, report O1.1): the 30 recorded briefs of the AR4 acceptance (auto-routing blueprint 2026-10-25, section 4.3 and the AR4 row). The briefs are the ones in plans/orchestration-2026-10-05/handoffs/msgs whose row in plans/lane-outcomes.tsv carries a recorded class, plus the website and research rows that keep the set at 30.",
	"_reading": "`paths` is each brief's owned paths, read from the brief's own 'Owned paths' line once by hand and resolved against the files the lane's merged commit touched in the crm-app repo, so every path is a real path of that repo. Where the brief names a group ('their tests under __tests__/', 'the shell files that mount the three surfaces'), the files the merged commit lists are recorded. `flags` holds only what the brief itself states: `perf` where the brief states class H5 performance, `causeUnknown` where it states class H2 with an unknown cause, `retry` where it states it is a second attempt or a redo of an earlier lane, `readsOnly` where it states it touches no other file. `class` is the recorded class of the lane-outcomes row (the brief's own class statement), and it is the expected value the rate is measured against.",
	"_project": "`project` is the project the brief works in, keyed into `routing.kindRules`. The canonical project id of the CRM app is `crm-app` (muster-projects.json). `research` and `website` have no kind patterns, so their briefs answer `unclear`: a project without patterns never guesses.",
	"_expectedKind": "`expectedKind` is the kind the shipped table must answer for that brief. It is the measurement: a pattern that changes a brief's kind fails the test, and a change to a kind needs a recorded decision, not a silent edit.",
